      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Dynamic images end up being raw textures, so 16mb or 23mb for a 2k texture, vs the X when it's dxt1 compressed. X is maybe like 5mb. I tried looking it up but I get a lot of distracting forum posts from 14 years ago.\n\nMy main point is that a world is more suitable for giving presentations. \n\nI guess if it's VRC+ feature and VRChat can allocate resources to compress to dxt1 and ASTC that'd work better, still, seems very messy.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
